  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure will bring above normal temps and \nmainly dry weather through early Saturday with above normal rain \nchances later Saturday through at least Sunday night along with\ncooler temps.\n\nHigh pressure will continue into early Sat keeping a warming trend \nthrough Fri night. Highs around 90 are likely inland today and\nFriday with humidity slowly continuing to increase. Rain chances\nwill be on the increase later Saturday as high pressure weakens,\na cold front approaches and moisture/upper forcing increase. \nRain chances should remain above normal through at least Sunday\nnight as the front slows down and lingers over or near the \narea. Trends favor a drier Monday, especially for northern/western\nareas, so confidence in the latest forecast rain chances is \nlow. At least there is a decent chance for beneficial rainfall \nover an inch, which would be very welcome considering the \nongoing drought in most areas. Still not expecting any appreciable\nsevere storm risk (mainly just on Sat), although locally heavy \nrainfall could produce minor flooding. \n\nMuch cooler and drier air should move in Mon night with below normal \ntemps (highs mainly in the low 70s and lows in the 40s/50s,\ncoldest Tue night when many inland areas could fall into the\n40s).",
